//? Title: Schreier–Sims: actual stabilizer orbits and checked group membership
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given permutation generators, compute their finite group order and a stabilizer
chain for membership tests. The report starts with S3, retains the original
symmetric, dihedral and alternating group examples, and displays actual S6 orbit
sizes.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

An orbit transversal chooses u_beta mapping the current base point to beta. For
generator s, the Schreier element u_(s(beta)) inverse composed with s composed
with u_beta fixes that base point. Sifting and adding nonidentity residues
closes the successive stabilizers. Orbit–stabilizer then gives
$$ |G|=\prod_i |\operatorname{Orb}_{G_i}(b_i)|. $$
\alttext(The group order is the product of actual orbit sizes along the stabilizer chain.)
The implementation checks this product for integer overflow. Sorted orbit
snapshots give deterministic traversal; the actual number of algebra operations
depends on generated residues and restarts, rather than a factorial enumeration
of members.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/schreier_sims_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/schreier_sims.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::schreier_sims_trace(3, a::symmetric_group_generators(3));
    std::print("| actual chain level | base point | orbit size |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < r.group.base.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", i, r.group.base[i],
                   r.group.transversal[i].size());
    std::print("\nActual discoveries {}, sifts {}.\n", r.discoveries.size(),
               r.sifts);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "S3: transposition and cycle");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("Actual levels {}", r.group.base.size()));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual group order {}", r.group.order));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/schreier_sims_tiny.svg");
}
```
